  "title": "86: al-Taariq الطارق",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nوَالسَّمَآءِ وَالطَّارِقِۙ‏(1)\nWAS SAMAAA-E WAT TAAREQE.\nBy the Sky and the Night-Visitant (therein);- \nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا الطَّارِقُۙ‏(2)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAT-TAAREQUN.\nAnd what will explain to thee what the Night-Visitant is? \nالنَّجْمُ الثَّاقِبُۙ‏(3)\nNAJMUS SAAQEBO.\n(It is) the Star of piercing brightness;- \nاِنْ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ لَّمَّا عَلَيْهَا حَافِظٌؕ‏(4)\nIN KULLO NAFSIL LAMMAA A’LAYHAA HAAFEZ.\nThere is no soul but has a protector over it. \nفَلْيَنْظُرِ الْاِنْسَانُ مِمَّ خُلِقَؕ‏(5)\nFAL-YANZORIL INSAANO MIMMA KHOLEQ.\nNow let man but think from what he is created! \nخُلِقَ مِنْ مَّآءٍ دَافِقٍۙ‏(6)\nKHOLEQA MIM MAAA-IN DAAFEQIN-Y.\nHe is created from a drop emitted- \nيَّخْرُجُ مِنْۢ بَيْنِ الصُّلْبِ وَالتَّرَآئِبِؕ‏(7)\nYAKHROJO MIM BAYNIS SULBE WAT TARAAA-EB.\nProceeding from between the backbone and the ribs: \nاِنَّهٗ عَلٰى رَجْعِهٖ لَقَادِرٌؕ‏(8)\nINNAHU A’LAA RAJ-E’HI LA-QAADER.\nSurely (Allah) is able to bring him back (to life)! \nيَوْمَ تُبْلَى السَّرَآئِرُۙ‏(9)\nYAWMA TUBLAS SARAAA-ERO.\nThe Day that (all) things secret will be tested, \nفَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ قُوَّةٍ وَّلَا نَاصِرٍؕ‏(10)\nFAMAA LAHU MIN QUWWATINW WA LAA NAASER.\n(Man) will have no power, and no helper. \nوَالسَّمَآءِ ذَاتِ الرَّجْعِۙ‏(11)\nWAS SAMAAA-E ZAATIR RAJ-E’.\nBy the Firmament which returns (in its round), \nوَالْاَرْضِ ذَاتِ الصَّدْعِۙ‏(12)\nWAL ARZE ZAATIS SAD-E’.\nAnd by the Earth which opens out (for the gushing of springs or the sprouting of vegetation), \nاِنَّهٗ لَقَوْلٌ فَصْلٌۙ‏(13)\nINNAHU LA-QAWLUN FASLUNW.\nBehold this is the Word that distinguishes (Good from Evil): \nوَّمَا هُوَ بِالْهَزْلِؕ‏(14)\nWA MAA HOWA BIL-HAZL.\nIt is not a thing for amusement. \nاِنَّهُمْ يَكِيْدُوْنَ كَيْدًا ۙ‏(15)\nINNAHUM YAKEEDOONA KAYDAANW.\nAs for them, they are but plotting a scheme, \nوَّاَكِيْدُ كَيْدًا ۚۖ‏(16)\nWA AKEEDO KAYDAA.\nAnd I am planning a scheme. \nفَمَهِّلِ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ اَمْهِلْهُمْ رُوَيْدًا‏(17)\nFA-MAH-HELIL KAAFEREENA AMHILHUM ROWAYDAA.\nTherefore grant a delay to the Unbelievers: Give respite to them gently (for awhile). ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Taariq (The Night-Comer)\nThis Surah has 17 verses and it is a ‘Makki’ Surah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the reward for reciting this Surah is equivalent to ten times the number of heavenly bodies in space.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has narrated that if Surah al-Taariq is recited in compulsory prayers, then the reciter is honoured by Allah (s.w.t.) and will get the opportunity of being with the Prophets (a.s.). Reciting this Surah over anything keeps it safe. If recited before taking medicine, then the medicine will be a sure cure. The water in which this Surah has been dissolved should be poured gently on a wound and it will heal with the Grace of Allah (s.w.t.)."
